DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("4*(sqrt(x))");
$fun_1 = Formula("cos((x-2))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(2, infinity) U (9, infinity)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (2, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (5, infinity))");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("(5, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (2, infinity)) U (9, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[2, infinity) U [2, infinity) U [2, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("((-infinity, 17) U (-infinity, 17)) U (-infinity, 17) U {-6, -5, -1, 8, 9, 10}");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-6, -5, -1, 8, 9, 10} U [2, infinity) U (-infinity, 17)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`5.72+6.22+11+18.18`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('41.12'),width=>9}
---

[`12.27+5.31+8+2.43`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('28.01'),width=>3}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 17\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 2\}`]
- [`C = \{-6, -5, -1, 8, 9, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(A \cup A) \cup A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`C \cup B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 1\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 4\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`B \cap A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, 10, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 3, 7, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -10, -9, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, 7, 6>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, 10, -2>") x Compute("<3, 7, 6>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, 7, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-9, 10, -2>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 7, 6>") . Compute("<-9, 10, -2>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 0, 7, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, -9, -10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, -9, -10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -9, -10>") x Compute("<0, 7, -4>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, -9, -10>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-4, -9, -10>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, 7, -4>") . Compute("<-4, -9, -10>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, 7, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>0)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
